    "result_text": "Done. The change is implemented and the test suite is green.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe membership-level derivation in `OwnerMapper.membershipLevel` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`) previously hard-capped every owner at level 3 with the comment that \"level 4 is reserved for tenure\" \u2014 but tenure was never actually implemented, so level 4 was unreachable.\n\nI added the tenure factor:\n\n- **+1 to the level when the owner's tenure is more than 365 days**, where tenure is the day count from `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` (via `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between`), and raised the cap to 4.\n- Guarded against a null `registrationDate`.\n- Updated the Javadoc to describe levels 1\u20134 and the tenure rule.\n\n## Why a new owner still lands at level 3\n\nOn create, `OwnerRestControllerV1` sets `registrationDate` to today, so tenure is 0 days \u2014 not greater than 365 \u2014 and the tenure factor doesn't apply. The test's owner (email present \u2192 +1, `namesakeCount` 0 \u2192 +1, base 1) therefore computes to **level 3, not 4**, exactly as the existing `AcceptanceTest.coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` asserts.\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
